        "timestamp": 182825416,
        "network": "FARCASTER_NETWORK_MAINNET",
        "castAddBody": {
          "embedsDeprecated": [],
          "mentions": [3],
          "parentCastId": null,
          "parentUrl": null,
          "text": "Some quick(ish) thoughts on people asking how I can support crops and be excited about the changes to Farcaster\n \nFarcaster (the app) has always had moderation and a social contract.  talked about moderation from the beginning. Having rules for an app doesn\u2019t inherently conflict with free speech or censorship resistance\n\nWe don\u2019t allow shitposting on ethresearch. It\u2019s a space for Ethereum research, and moderation helps keep it useful. That\u2019s reasonable. If the mods started banning research about MEV because they personally didn\u2019t think MEV was a problem, that would be a different story. They\u2019d be using their position to suppress ideas within the discussion the forum is supposed to support\n\nI\u2019m directionally for apps experimenting with rules and algorithms that make conversations more productive. We already have algorithms deciding what gets attention, based on what keeps us scrolling. I want people trying other approaches\n\n1/3",
          "embeds": [],
          "mentionsPositions": [183],
          "type": "LONG_CAST"
        }
      },
